   "outcomes": [
    "Demonstrate an understanding of how the concepts of race, racism, ethnicity, white supremacy, imperialism, prejudice, and discrimination have manifested and impacted the lives of Asian Americans in an historical overview.",
    "Describe the critical events, histories, cultures, and social struggles of immigrants and refugees from regions in Asia and the resulting impact on the challenges and social progress of the Asian American movement in the United States.",
    "Examine how Asian Americans have struggled for racial and social justice, solidarity, and liberation in relation to other historically marginalized racial groups and how these struggles are relevant to current and structural social issues.",
    "Critically analyze aspects of cultural practices of diverse Asian American ethnic groups and explain how they are relevant to issues, dilemmas, and problems encountered by Asian Americans in their lives today.",
    "Explore how Asian Americans have maintained cultural identity and preserved or transformed cultural practices within the intersection of acculturation, assimilation, and generation in America."
